### The finale: the hack, the choice, the endings.
### Launched from Mr. Robot at the arcade once the pieces are gathered.

=== finale_check
-- start
? !flag.joined_fsociety -> notready
? !flag.rootkit_planted -> need_rootkit
? !q.mq_steel.done -> need_steel
? !q.mq_darkarmy.done -> need_whiterose
? !q.mq_fbi>=20 -> need_fbi
? !flag.ecorp_door_tyrell & !flag.ecorp_foothold -> need_door
? !q.mq_robot.done -> need_truth
? !flag.ally_secured -> need_ally
-> ready
-- notready
MR. ROBOT: You're not even one of us yet, kid. Join fsociety first. Then we talk about ending the world's debt.
-> END
-- need_rootkit
MR. ROBOT: We've got no foothold. Ron's server, the rootkit: that's the first thread. Pull it before you dream about the tapestry.
-> END
-- need_steel
MR. ROBOT: The backups. Steel Mountain. Until those tapes are ash, encrypting E Corp's records is like erasing a chalkboard someone photographed. Go cook the mountain.
-> END
-- need_whiterose
MR. ROBOT: You haven't sat in the clock room yet. Whether we take her army or not, you look Whiterose in the eye before we do this. I won't press a key on a night she's planned without us knowing what she wants.
-> END
-- need_fbi
MR. ROBOT: There's a Fed in the city who has said your name out loud. DiPierro. Go see her. Lie to her, use her, or tell her the truth, but don't let her be a surprise on the night.
-> END
-- need_door
MR. ROBOT: We need inside the tower. Tyrell hands us the keys, or you take a keycard off a guard and let yourself in. No inside man, no Five/Nine.
-> END
-- need_truth
? q.mq_robot.started -> need_truth_started
MR. ROBOT: ...Darlene wants to talk to you first. Go. I'll be here. I'm always here.
-> END
-- need_truth_started
MR. ROBOT: Finish it, kid. The photo, the sign, the hospital, the pier. You don't press the biggest key in history without knowing whose hand is on it.
-> END
-- need_ally
MR. ROBOT: We've got no army. No Dark Army, no blind Bureau. We can still go. It'll be five people and a soldering iron against the biggest company on Earth, and if anything breaks we fix it live with nobody covering us.
* "Then we go alone. Like it started." -> alone
* "Not yet. Let me find us an army." -> END
-- alone
MR. ROBOT: That's my kid. Five people and a soldering iron. Some nights that's all a revolution ever was.
! set ally_secured ; set ally_alone
-> ready
-- ready
MR. ROBOT: Look at me. Everything's in place. The rootkit, the mountain, the army, the door. This is it. This is the night we've been walking toward your whole life. Are you ready to press the key?
* "Do it. Encrypt everything. Free them." -> hack
* "Wait. Once I do this, there's no undo." -> wait
* [require stab<30] "Are you even real? Am I about to blow up the world because a voice in my head told me to?" -> doubt
-- wait
MR. ROBOT: There's never an undo, kid. That's what makes it a choice instead of a rehearsal. Come back when your hands stop shaking. Or don't. Shaking hands still type.
-> END
-- doubt
MR. ROBOT: Real. Not real. Wrong question. The debt is real. The people crushed under it are real. This key is real. Press it and it doesn't matter what I am. It only matters what you did. That's the only honesty left.
! glitch 0.7 ; stab 5
-> hack
-- hack
> You run the exploit. E Corp's records, seventy percent of the world's consumer debt, begin to encrypt behind a key that will exist for exactly as long as it takes to throw it away.
! minigame cascade
? won -> hacked
MR. ROBOT: The cascade broke. Steady your hands and run it again — we don't get a second window like this.
-> ready
-- hacked
> Progress bars crawl toward 100%. Somewhere, a mortgage becomes a rumor. A student loan becomes a story. The number that ruled millions of lives becomes noise.
MR. ROBOT: It's done. It's actually done. Five/Nine.
! set five_nine_done ; quest mq_finale 30 ; quest mq_after 10 ; xp 300 ; fame fsociety 10 ; glitch 1.0
? flag.ms_done -> games
? flag.rs_done -> gamers
-> home
-- games
> On a phone propped against a dead arcade cabinet, the Respawn forum refreshes itself over and over. Thirty thousand people, posting the same three words. PRESS START, FRIEND.
MR. ROBOT: Your gamers are watching. Microslop tried to teach them nobody owns anything. You just taught them nobody owes anything either. Same lesson, kid. Louder.
-> home
-- gamers
> Somewhere on the arcade floor a phone buzzes with a forum notification: Pixel, in all caps, saying nothing but OH MY GOD, over and over.
-> home
-- home
MR. ROBOT: Go home, kid. Sleep, if you can. Turn on the news in the morning. Then we find out what we actually did.
-> END

=== finale_choose
### Reached at the Salina after the deus table. Resolves the ending.
-- start
? flag.ending_path=overlap -> overlap_path
? flag.ending_path=deus -> deus_path
? flag.ending_path=defy -> defy_path
-> pick
-- pick
ELLIOT (V.O.): The hack is done. The city is already changing outside. Now I decide who I hand the smoke to.
* "fsociety keeps it. The debt stays dead. We disappear." -> e_fsociety
* [require flag.da_allied] "Let Whiterose finish it her way. Her timetable, her ending." -> e_darkarmy
* [require flag.fbi_informant | flag.fbi_bigger | flag.price_fbi] "I give the FBI everything. Clean hands. Let the law sort the rubble." -> e_fbi
* [require flag.ecorp_door_tyrell] "I take E Corp's offer. A seat at the table. Power, not a basement." -> e_ecorp
* "None of them. I destroy the key and the records both. No masters. Just gone." -> e_reboot
* [require flag.township_public | flag.ecoin_exposed] "All of it goes to the press. The hack, the Township memos, E Coin, this table, every name. Let the world decide." -> e_press
* [require stab<25 | flag.robot_rejected & stab<45] "...I'm tired. You do it. Let him have it." -> e_robot
* [require flag.kingpin] "When the banks go dark, cash is king. And I own the cash." -> e_kingpin
* [require innocents>=12] "Let it burn. The records, the city, all of them. It's what I'm for now." -> e_monster
-- overlap_path
ELLIOT (V.O.): There's a version of tonight where nobody has to lose. Where Darlene's still my sister, and Krista's truth is out, and the whole broken family of this city stands in one room and refuses to be sorted. I saw the seam. I can pull it.
* [require flag.darlene_bond & flag.knows_darlene_sister & flag.krista_truth & stab>=60 & !flag.robot_rejected] "We do it together. All of us. The Overlap." -> e_overlap
* "...No. That's a dream. Pick a real ending." -> pick
-- deus_path
ELLIOT (V.O.): I already sat at their table and nodded. The ending they wanted is the ending they get. I tell myself I'm the exception. Everyone at that table told themselves that once.
-> e_ecorp
-- defy_path
ELLIOT (V.O.): I looked the men who own the world in the eye and told them no. Now I have to make the no mean something.
* "fsociety keeps it. The debt stays dead." -> e_fsociety
* "Destroy it all. No masters." -> e_reboot
* [require flag.township_public | flag.ecoin_exposed] "Give everything to the press." -> e_press
-- e_fsociety
! ending fsociety
-> END
-- e_darkarmy
! ending darkarmy
-> END
-- e_fbi
! ending fbi
-> END
-- e_ecorp
! ending ecorp
-> END
-- e_reboot
! ending reboot
-> END
-- e_press
! ending press
-> END
-- e_robot
ELLIOT (V.O.): I stop holding on. It's so easy. He's been waiting at the edge of every thought for years. He steps in, and his hand closes around mine, and it's his hand now.
MR. ROBOT: Good kid. I've got it from here.
! ending robot
-> END
-- e_kingpin
ELLIOT (V.O.): The world's debt is gone. Every card declines, every bank is dark. And nine corners in the Bronx still take cash, and the cash comes to me.
! ending kingpin
-> END
-- e_monster
ELLIOT (V.O.): I used to tell myself they were bad people. Then I stopped telling myself anything. The debt was never the point. The point was how quiet it gets, after.
! ending monster
-> END
-- e_overlap
! ending overlap
-> END
